WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.616
Many integer defects are API design defects.

2
00:00:02.616 --> 00:00:12.334
A function parameter named size, length, count, offset, or limit may look clear to the original author, but the next caller may not know the unit,

3
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.951
valid range, ownership rule, or failure behavior.

4
00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:18.688
The API should make those facts as visible as possible.

5
00:00:18.688 --> 00:00:22.426
Avoid casually mixing counts, bytes, indexes, capacities, offsets, and timeouts.

6
00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:27.659
If two values have different units, the code should not make them look interchangeable.

7
00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:35.508
Domain-specific wrapper types, clearer names, and small validation functions can help maintain the distinction without making ordinary code hard to

8
00:00:35.508 --> 00:00:35.881
read.

9
00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:41.488
Checked arithmetic helpers are useful for operations that influence allocation, indexing, serialization, or resource limits.

10
00:00:41.488 --> 00:00:48.216
A helper can centralize the precondition check and return a result that forces the caller to handle failure.

11
00:00:48.216 --> 00:00:53.822
This reduces repeated hand-written checks and gives reviewers a familiar pattern to look for.

12
00:00:53.822 --> 00:00:58.307
Explicit failure behavior is safer than silent truncation or ambiguous sentinel values.

13
00:00:58.307 --> 00:01:08.025
If a conversion cannot be represented, if a calculation exceeds the allowed range, or if output does not fit, the API should say how callers learn

14
00:01:08.025 --> 00:01:08.773
that fact.

15
00:01:08.773 --> 00:01:15.501
Return values, exceptions, optional results, status objects, or project-standard error handling can all work when applied consistently.

16
00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:18.491
Good APIs make risky decisions easy to find.

17
00:01:18.491 --> 00:01:24.097
Conversions, unit changes, range narrowing, and size calculations should not be hidden in long expressions.

18
00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:32.320
When the code shows intent directly, reviewers can focus on whether the rule is correct instead of reverse-engineering the numeric path.
